WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
Imagine waking up to find that every
dollar in the country has doubled.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.900
Your paycheck doubles.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.430
Your savings double.

4
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.300
So does everyone else's money.

5
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.120
Are you twice as rich?

6
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.260
Or does a burger now cost twice as much?

7
00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:17.230
So if a country printed
twice as much money,

8
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.920
would everything really
cost twice as much?

9
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.880
In this mission, you'll use one
equation to calculate the money supply,

10
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.580
velocity, the price level and real GDP.

11
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.290
Then you'll double the
money supply on a graph,

12
00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.380
and track real GDP and the price level.

13
00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: figure out what really
happens when the money supply doubles.
